pc|SJ|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I could lead a club, partner's suit. But I know West is short. So a trump lead seems better, although given West has 5 trump, probably makes little difference.|
PG| ***** 8 ***** |


pc|S2|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|North knows I have only 1 spade. So North has no reason to duck the spade. In fact, given his club length, North should take the @SA and return a spade. By the way, if North wants to lead a club, the correct lead is the @CK from @CAK in the middle of the hand. Playing the @CA denies the @CK.|
PG| ***** 9 ***** |


