up|52|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|So remember that in a competitive auction, a jump raise is weak. You cue bid to show a limit+ raise or, in this case, since West knows they want to be in game, |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=splinters,Splinter^*N|CP||FP||at| bid is good, in case they should be in slam. |

n#|9|at|^^^fIf you do follow the link you can return  HERE  by clicking the  |fp|1|n#|3|at|@L|fp||n^|3|at|   icon button, top left.|
PG| ***** 22 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Note that with the same hand and a doubleton (rather than singleton club), West should first bid 3@C (showing a limit+ raise with 3+ spades) and then bid 4@S. Many players would jump to 4@S, but that shows a weak hand with 5 spades. West needs to show a strong hand by either cue bidding with no shortness or making a |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=splinters,Splinter^*N|CP||FP||at| bid with a strong hand and shortness.|

n#|9|at|^^^fIf you do follow the link you can return  HERE  by clicking the  |fp|1|n#|3|at|@L|fp||n^|3|at|   icon button, top left.|
PG| ***** 23 ***** |


