qx|A2|st||rh||ah|Board 2 IMPs   -   April 17, 2024|pn|hondo717,Rustgi65,Honeydog3,danpsych|
md|4SKHAK5DAJT95CAQ98,ST8632HJ3DK86CT72,SAQ4H97642D7CK543,SJ975HQT8DQ432CJ6|sv|n|
mb|P|MB|?|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I never open Notrump with a singleton. However, over a 2@C opener I will follow 2N with a singleton ace or king. It is a bit risky but it gets the strength across which you otherwise could not do. I could open 2@C and then bid 3@D over 2@D but that takes up an awful lot of room.|
PG| ***** 25 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|This hand has ostensibly 21 HCP, so technically you could open it 2N. Admittedly you can subtract 1 for the singleton King but with 4.5 |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=quicktricks,Quick Tricks^*N|CP||FP||at|, a quality diamond suit, and a near quality club suit the hand is worth more than 21. So I am going to open 2@C and rebid 2N to show 22-24.|

n#|9|at|^^^fIf you do follow the link you can return  HERE  by clicking the  |fp|1|n#|3|at|@L|fp||n^|3|at|   icon button, top left.|
PG| ***** 26 ***** |


mb|2C|mb|P|mb|2D|mb|P|mb|2N|an|22-24|
pg| ***** 27 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|P|mb|3D|an|Hearts|
PG| ***** 28 ***** |


mb|P|MB|?|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Normally in this position, I would only jump to 4@H with 4-card support. However, @HAKx is just about the best 3-card support I could have and I am a bit worried about my singleton @SK. So I am going to cheat and bid 4@H. By the way, I think North should have tried for slam. I have 22-24 and let's count North's |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=declarerpoints,Bergen Declarer Points^*N|CP||FP||at|.|
PG| ***** 29 ***** |


mb|4h|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|North has 9 HCP, 1 length point, and declarer addons of 2 for the singleton and 1 for the side 4-card club suit for 13 points. That is more than enough to try for slam. Further, 4@H took up an awful lot of room so I would just bid RKCB to try for slam.|
PG| ***** 30 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^^B@2^*BA Kibitzer: ^*nBut North is not declarer.|
PG| ***** 31 ***** |


cp|8|AT|^^
^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Yes. It is true that North is not declarer. However, the way |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=bergenhandevaluation,Bergen Hand Evaluation^*N|CP||FP||at| works is, you count ^*BDeclarer Points^*n in the hand with the long suit because typically the hand with the long suit bids the suit first.|
PG| ***** 32 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Perhaps a different way to describe Bergen's ^*BDeclarer Points^*n is counting points for the hand with the longer trump. You need to keep in mind is that, when there is a transfer bid, the hand that made the transfer should count |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=declarerpoints,Bergen Declarer Points^*N|CP||FP||at|.|
PG| ***** 33 ***** |


mb|P|mb|P|mb|P|
pg| ***** 34 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|sk|s|
pc|S2|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|As you can see, if clubs and heart break, we have only one heart loser and slam will make thereby once again verifying that Bergen Hand Evaluation is pretty accurate on most hands.|
PG| ***** 35 ***** |


