cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|The reason I am playing the clubs this way is that if the @C10 or @CJ appears on the first round I can handle a 4-1 break in either direction. Say for example West had played the @C10 then I would assume it is possible that East started with Jxxx and I can lead a club to dummy and finesse East.|
PG| ***** 40 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Similar logic if East played the @CJ or @C10 I would play the @CQ and finesse West for the club if necessary.|
PG| ***** 41 ***** |


